From a08df818f0b93c155cd6e946277cf86b755c9e1c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wisang Drillian Geni <gwisang45@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 20:24:39 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] Fake touch inputs for select apps

Based on "Core: Add force mouse click as touch toggle"

For packages listed in persist.waydroid.fake_touch, a primary-button
mouse gesture is delivered as a finger gesture: tool type FINGER, no
button state, source TOUCHSCREEN. Hover events and primary
BUTTON_PRESS/RELEASE are dropped, since a finger has neither. Right and
middle clicks and the scroll wheel stay mouse input.

Rewriting only the source is not enough: WebView (Chromium's
EventForwarder) sends any event whose tool type is MOUSE and whose
button state is non-zero down the mouse path, so touch-only pages
never see the click.

Co-authored-by: Alessandro Astone <ales.astone@gmail.com>
Co-authored-by: Umang96 <umangleekha3@gmail.com>
Change-Id: Ibe26a1cdc41744ad201427093ec384b9a5a0e4b2
---
 core/java/android/view/ViewRootImpl.java | 94 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 94 insertions(+)

